=== NEXT UP (priority order) ===
Highest visible-return / in-flight work first:
1. Post-processing: bloom + tone mapping (easy, dramatic; slots into composite pass)
2. Ambient occlusion / SSAO
3. Dynamic skybox + atmospheric scattering (pairs with sun direction)
4. Omni shadow pass optimization (~2ms with many lights) + raise maxShadowLights
5. Cascades: get rid of geometry shader (perf)
6. Greedy meshing, then evaluate marching cubes


=== RENDERING & LIGHTING ===
- lights
    - sun / directional @done
    - point - omnidirectional (using cubemap?) @done
        - optimize omni shadow pass (caps ~2ms with many shadow lights):
            - cache cube maps: re-render a light's depth only when it moves or a chunk within its radius is re-meshed; skip+don't-clear clean lights. Requires STABLE light->layer slots (shadowIndex is currently re-sorted by camera distance every frame, which churns the layer and breaks caching)
            - per-light geometry culling: each shadow light currently draws the whole shared omni shadow buffer (chunks near ANY light); cull to only chunks within THIS light's radius (could lean on ClusterBuild light/cluster assignments)
            - stagger updates: re-render only K lights/frame round-robin instead of all. Same foundation as caching (needs stable light->layer slots + per-layer clear instead of clearing the whole array). Pairs with raising maxShadowLights since it bounds per-frame cost regardless of light count
            - raise maxShadowLights (8 feels low); drop shadow res 1024->512 to afford more VRAM (1024^2 depth cube ~= 24MB/light)
